{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: assert the stamp comes after the stage in ci.yml**

The retargeted guard checks that ci.yml contains both `stage_publish_package.sh /tmp/pr-dry-run-stage` (line 568) and `stamp_staged_release.sh /tmp/pr-dry-run-stage "$next"` (line 576) — but as two independent `contains`/`indexOf` assertions. A future edit could place the stamp before the stage (or in a different job/step) and this guard would still pass, even though `stamp_staged_release.sh` would then fail at runtime on a missing staged pubspec.

